    "lawCode": "Amd §143, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3364\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to deposits on\nplans and specifications for contracts for public works\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation makes permissive the requirement for deposits that\nState agencies currently must charge for bidders to obtain copies of\nplans and specifications for public works projects.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends State Finance Law (SFL) § 143 to require\ndeposits on plans and specifications for contracts for public works\nfor minority and women-owned business enterprises on request, and\npermit such waiver where plans and specifications are made available\nin non-paper form.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nSFL § 143 requires a deposit to be made by bidders with the\ncontracting agency for purposes of obtaining plans and specifications\nfor public works projects and for return of this material and the\ndeposit.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThese amendments were introduced in 2005 in the Senate (S.4205) and in\n2007 in the Assembly and the Senate (A.8523/S.4002-A) but did not\nadvance out of committee.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nIn preparation for bidding a construction project, over a hundred\ncopies of drawings and specifications are prepared for distribution on\na per-contract basis and inventoried for distribution. Prospective\nbidders and suppliers then must purchase the bid documents directly\nfrom the State agency pursuant to statute. Since drawings and\nspecifications are now produced electronically, printing and shipping\nlarge drawings and books of specifications is more costly than\ncommunicating this information for distribution electronically.\n\nThis bill will enable State agencies to waive the requirement of a\ndeposit for bid documents where such documents are produced and\navailable electronically or for certified minority and women owned\nbusiness enterprises pursuant to Executive Law Article 15-A.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :\n\nMinimal.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
